8205635249614716, 0.013195502571761608, -0.00032142087002284825, 0.016299061477184296, -0.0265200212597847, 0.026606032624840736, -0.021732082590460777, 0.015252595767378807, 0.020026199519634247, -0.032540783286094666, -0.010521997697651386, 0.036669306457042694, 0.02588927373290062, 0.03245477005839348, 0.003995921928435564, 0.0068522002547979355, -0.01604102924466133, -0.011052398011088371, 0.0033311296720057726, 0.007178324740380049], "index": 8, "object": "embedding"}], "model": "text-embedding-3-small", "object": "list", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 7173, "total_tokens": 7173}}, "input": {"input": ["Collector.java:96)  Corrupted subaccounts could not be loaded properly. As a consequence, it was impossible to delete them from the administration UI. In some cases, they even did not appear in the list of subaccounts, but were existing, so trying to add such a subaccount would fail.This issue has been fixed.      Self-signed system certificates containing SANs need to have all CA attributes, which is not desired for the system certificate, and hence it does not have them. As a consequence, such a certificate cannot be added to the trust store of a server, which is needed to establish trust. By not allowing to add SAN elements to self-signed system certificates, this problem can no longer occur.      A denial of service vulnerability in the Cloud Connector was fixed.For more information, see security note https://me.sap.com/notes/3362463.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2023-11-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3844 ---\nComponent: Connectivity\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Cloud Connector 2.16.1 - Enhancements\nDescription: Release of Cloud Connector version 2.16.1 provides the following enhancement:  The subaccount dashboard now allows to sort the entries based on the display name.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2023-11-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3845 ---\nComponent: Multitarget Applications for Cloud Foundry\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Bug fixes and improvements\nDescription:   Add MTA metadata attributes to user-provided service instances. This will improve MTA discovery of org.cloudfoundry.user-provided-service type of resources.  You can now preserve app environment after blue-green deployment with MTA Module parameter keep-existing and its option env. For more information see CF-MTA-Examples.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-06\nValid as Of: 2023-11-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3846 ---\nComponent: Multitarget Applications for Cloud Foundry\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Features and improvements\nDescription:     Improved performance and usability of deployment with MTA archive URL. In order to use the latest improvements it is necessary for you to update your multiapps plugin to the latest 3.3.1 version.       Improved user experience when sharing your service instances using the Service Manager functionality and consuming it afterwards by resolving ${service-guid} as a cross mta configuration.      Large MTA archive processing on GCP environments is enabled. The limit on MTA archives has been expanded from 1GB to 4GBs.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-06\nValid as Of: 2023-11-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3847 ---\nComponent: SAP Alert Notification Service\nEnvironment: Other\nTitle: A new section has been added\nDescription: You can now find information about the Security Recommendations related to the SAP Alert Notification service.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-22\nValid as Of: 2023-11-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3848 ---\nComponent: SAP Alert Notification Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New SAP HANA Cloud Service Database Events\nDescription: You can now use the newly supported HDB Last Infrastructure Operation and HDB Template Recovery events.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-22\nValid as Of: 2023-11-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3849 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Change to Cloud Foundry API Rate Limit Reset Interval\nDescription: The Cloud Foundry API rate limit configuration has been changed from about 40.000 requests per user per hour to a new limit of around 20.000 requests per user per 30 minutes.   This change is made to prevent the CF API peak load from having a negative impact on the availability of the CF API.   The overall CF API rate limits have not been changed.   Please note that the CF API rate limit reset interval is planned to be further reduced in the future.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-16\nValid as Of: 2023-11-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3850 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 32.17.0\nDescription: Cloud Foundry has been updated from version 32.13.0 to 32.17.0.      https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v32.17.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v32.16.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v32.15.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v32.14.0    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New", "://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v32.17.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v32.16.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v32.15.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v32.14.0    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-16\nValid as Of: 2023-11-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 1911 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: New Class Interface for Application Job Catalog Entries and Templates\nDescription: You can now work with a new attribute-based class interface. With the new class interface, you can now change the parameters, sections, and groups of a catalog entry. Value helps are now supported and can be selected in the catalog entry parameters. You can also run a class for testing in the application job template.  See Working with Application Job Objects.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1912 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Rerunning Unit Tests with Coverage\nDescription: You can now rerun unit tests with coverage in the ABAP Coverage view.  See Evaluating ABAP Unit Code Coverage Results.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1913 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Triggering Where-Used List for Usages of CDS Annotation\nDescription: You can now trigger a where-used search also for CDS annotations. This enables you to investigate in which ABAP CDS objects an annotation is used.  The result is displayed in the Search view. From the integrated toolbar, you filter and change how the result is displayed. By double-clicking the finding, you can navigate to the relevant usage.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1914 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: abapGit: Support of Object Deletions\nDescription: Object deletions can be exported from and imported to the ABAP environment with abapGit.  For more information, see Object Deletions with abapGit.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-16\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1915 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: APIs for Customer-Managed Security Settings\nDescription: The system exposes APIs to retrieve customer-managed security settings in a read-only manner.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1916 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Approve ATC Exemptions App: Change Validity Date for ATC Exemptions in the Approve ATC Exemptions App\nDescription: As a processor of an exemption, you can now change its validity date. You no longer have to be the creator of the examption request to do this.  See Approve ATC Exemptions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1917 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Approve ATC Exemptions App: Replication of ATC Exemptions from On-Premise Towards SAP BTP\nDescription: You can now replicate ATC exemptions from your on-premise ATC system to the ATC in SAP BTP. Customers need to use transaction SATC_EXPORT_XMPT to download the exemptions from an on-premise ATC system.  See Enable Usage of the Approve ATC Exemptions App.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1918 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Automated Handling for Default Client Certificates\nDescription: SAP BTP ABAP environment tenants are now equipped with a signed default client certificate, which is automatically rotated and can be used for customer managed integration scenarios.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1919 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Business Event Logging\nDescription: With Business Event Logging, you can capture and log business events locally within the ABAP environment. It includes:      The business event log: A persistence of raised business events in the ABAP system.      The Activate Business Event Logging configuration item to activate logging on an object level.      UI apps to view the business event log.      CDS views to access the business event logs.      Communication scenario SAP_COM_0A54 to externally access and replicate data to other applications.     ", "\nDescription: With Business Event Logging, you can capture and log business events locally within the ABAP environment. It includes:      The business event log: A persistence of raised business events in the ABAP system.      The Activate Business Event Logging configuration item to activate logging on an object level.      UI apps to view the business event log.      CDS views to access the business event logs.      Communication scenario SAP_COM_0A54 to externally access and replicate data to other applications.      The Direct Logging API to create direct entries to the business event log from your ABAP environment.      For more information, see Business Event Logging.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-10\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1920 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Business Rule Framework Plus\nDescription: The Business Rule Framework plus (BRFplus) is enhanced with the following:     Code Generation service: With this new feature, BRFplus functions can now utilize a code template service for automatic code generation.      An API introduced to facilitate the consumption of business rules within ABAP Cloud.      For more information, see API for Consumption of Business Rules.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n", "--- Record 2031 ---\nComponent: Connectivity\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Cloud Connector - New Regions\nDescription: Additional regions were added to SAP BTP:    ap30: Australia (Sydney) - Google Cloud  br20: Brazil (São Paulo) - Azure  sa30: KSA (Dammam) - Google Cloud    For more information, see Cloud Connector: Prerequisites.  In case of questions please contact SAP Support.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-28\nValid as Of: 2024-10-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2032 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Bug Fix for Application Name in the SAP Fiori for ABAP Platform Pipeline\nDescription: In the release stage of the SAP Fiori for ABAP Platform pipeline, the namespace prefixes are available again.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-28\nValid as Of: 2024-10-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2033 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: API Gateway module: Update to verison 2.7.0\nDescription: This release contains the following changes:     We've added support for short host name in version v2alpha1 of APIRule. If you only provide the leftmost label in the spec.hosts field of an APIRule custom resource (CR), it uses the domain name from the referenced Gateway, expanding the host to <label>.<gateway domain>. See Sample Custom Resources.      We've fixed the wildcard path format and the validation of the rule path in an APIRule.      Release 2.7 of the API Gateway module includes the fully functional version of APIRule v2alpha1 with noAuth, jwt, and extAuth access strategies. Version v2alpha1 is not meant for use in a production environment but for testing purposes only. After the rollout to the regular channel on October 28, 2024, you’ll be required to start testing the migration procedure. To learn more, see the APIRule migration blog post. It provides the timeline for deletion of APIRule v1beta1 and covers the following migration scenarios:  From the noop, allow, or no_authhandler in version v1beta1 to the noAuth handler in version v2alpha1  From the jwt handler in version v1beta1 to the new configuration of the jwt handler in version v2alpha1    The migration procedure from OAuth2 handlers based on Ory Oathkeeper to the new extAuth handler will be published in the next blog post. For now, see the tutorial Exposing a Workload with extAuth.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-03\nValid as Of: 2024-10-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2034 ---\nComponent: Region\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Australia (Sydney)\nDescription: Australia (Sydney) (cf-ap30) is available as a new region running on Google Cloud for use with enterprise accounts. See Regions and API Endpoints Available for the Cloud Foundry Environment.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-28\nValid as Of: 2024-10-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2035 ---\nComponent: Region\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Brazil (São Paulo)\nDescription: Brazil (São Paulo) (cf-br20) is available as a new region running on Azure for use with enterprise accounts. See Regions and API Endpoints Available for the Cloud Foundry Environment.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-28\nValid as Of: 2024-10-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2036 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP Task Center Improvements\nDescription: The following improvements are introduced for the SAP Task Center Web app:    Handling of attachments with IDs that include special characters      Support for opening task directly via deep links    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-28\nValid as Of: 2024-10-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2037 ---\nComponent: Data Space Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription: The following are the latest versions in Data Space Integration:      Data Space Integration: 1.1.*      Increment: 2409      Tractus-X Eclipse Dataspace Connector: 0.7.4      FOSS Eclipse Dataspace Components: 0.7.1      See also the Release Notesof Catena-X. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-26\nValid as Of: 2024-10-26\nVersion: 2409\n\n--- Record 2038 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Actions in Component Monitor\nDescription: You can now perform the following actions on components that support Diagnostics:    Create Heap Dump Diagnostic Task    Create Thread Dump Diagnostic Task  Choose the overflow menu to see all the available actions for the selected component.  See: Component Monitor\nAction: Info only", "26\nValid as Of: 2024-10-26\nVersion: 2409\n\n--- Record 2038 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Actions in Component Monitor\nDescription: You can now perform the following actions on components that support Diagnostics:    Create Heap Dump Diagnostic Task    Create Thread Dump Diagnostic Task  Choose the overflow menu to see all the available actions for the selected component.  See: Component Monitor\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-26\nValid as Of: 2024-10-26\nVersion: 2409\n\n--- Record 2039 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Actions Menu in Component Monitor\nDescription: The View Runtime Parameters and View Pod Events buttons have moved to the overflow menu.  See: Component Monitor\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-26\nValid as Of: 2024-10-26\nVersion: 2409\n\n--- Record 2040 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Cleanup Diagnostics Data Action in Job Management\nDescription: A new action, Cleanup Diagnostic Data, is now available in Job Management. You can create jobs with this action to delete manually created diagnostic tasks and automatically generated heap dumps. It also deletes empty working directories created by the Worker component on the shared file system that are no longer in use.  See: Job Management  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-26\nValid as Of: 2024-10-26\nVersion: 2409\n\n", "--- Record 3321 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Core\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Resource groups limit per tenant\nDescription: The maximum number of resource groups is limited at tenant level to 50. If you reach this limit, you receive an error message. To free up space, delete some resource groups. Alternatively, raise a ticket to increase your quota.  For more information, see Delete a Resource Group.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-08\nValid as Of: 2024-03-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3322 ---\nComponent: Availability Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Deprecation of Permissions APIs\nDescription: All /v1/permissions APIs are deprecated and will be retired with the 2408a release.  Please migrate to use /v1/groups/{groupId}/users APIs.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-07\nValid as Of: 2024-03-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3323 ---\nComponent: Availability Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Rescoped Visibility of Testers\nDescription: The option to switch visibility of testers of any type to public is disabled.  Newly created push testers must be private.  Testers of type ExpServPush can only be created by SysAdmins, public Site24x7 testers must be quota enabled.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-07\nValid as Of: 2024-03-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3324 ---\nComponent: Automation Pilot\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Example Scenarios\nDescription: New example commands were added to the Automation Pilot Samples Repository. They demonstrate the automation of various scenarios such as check HANA Cloud availability, stop/start all Cloud Foundry applications, and so on. See Example Scenarios.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-07\nValid as Of: 2024-03-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3325 ---\nComponent: Availability Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Option to Disable Certificate Chain Validation\nDescription: Site24x7 certificate monitors support an additional option to enable/disable certificate chain validation. This enables test scenarios with self-signed certificates or custom PKI setups.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-07\nValid as Of: 2024-03-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3326 ---\nComponent: Custom Domain Service\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: New Optional Parameter for list-custom-domain-mappings\nDescription: You can now use the optional parameter --ssl-host when running the list-custom-domain-mappings command. This parameter lets you filter custom domain mappings per given SSL host.  See list-custom-domain-mappings.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-07\nValid as Of: 2024-03-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3327 ---\nComponent: Forms Service by Adobe\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Service Plan Free\nDescription: The SAP Forms service now provides the following new feature:You can use service plan free to test and explore the features provided by the SAP Forms service.For more information, see SAP Forms Service by Adobe (SAP Discovery Center).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-03-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3328 ---\nComponent: HTML5 Applications\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Security Recommendations\nDescription: Security recommendations for the the application router have been published.   See SAP BTP Security Recommendations.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-07\nValid as Of: 2024-03-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3329 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: SAP BTP Operator becomes a default module\nDescription: SAP BTP Operator has been upgraded to a default Kyma module and is now automatically added to all new clusters. This enhancement ensures that Service Management is readily available. For more information, read the Kyma Modules document.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-07\nValid as Of: 2024-03-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3330 ---\nComponent: Object Store\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Azure: A new approach for auto-expiration rules deletion\nDescription: A new approach to delete an auto-expiration rule has been introduced. Please refer Auto Expiration of Blobs and Blob Versions for more details.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-07\nValid as Of: 2024-03-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 3351 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Event Triggers\nDescription: You can execute an event trigger by entering a single input parameter using the Run now action, without adding any additional details related to the cloud event. See Manage Event Triggers from the Triggers View.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-04\nValid as Of: 2024-03-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3352 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Outlook SDK\nDescription: You can use the Fetch Emails activity to retrieve emails from all Outlook mail accounts and initiate the process of fetching mails in Outlook. See Best Practices for Outlook Activities\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-04\nValid as Of: 2024-03-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3353 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Referenced SAPUI5 Version\nDescription: As part of hotfix collection 4, SAPUI5 version 1.120.8 is used for the administrator’s SAP Fiori launchpad, SAP-delivered Fiori apps, and the custom-built SAP Fiori apps, which are deployed to the ABAP system.  See SAP BTP ABAP Environment – Maintenance Windows and Major Upgrade Windows in 2024 and SAP UI5\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-11\nValid as Of: 2024-03-02\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2402\n\n--- Record 3354 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Referenced SAPUI5 Version\nDescription: As part of hotfix collection 4, SAPUI5 version 1.120.8 is used for the administrator’s SAP Fiori launchpad, SAP-delivered Fiori apps, and the custom-built SAP Fiori apps, which are deployed to the ABAP system.  See SAP BTP ABAP Environment – Maintenance Windows and Major Upgrade Windows in 2024 and SAP UI5\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-11\nValid as Of: 2024-03-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3355 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: A Save As New Project Option is Available for Action Projects\nDescription: We've introduced the Save As New Project feature in Actions. This feature allows you to create a copy of a finished action project so that you can start a new one with similar properties. Use this function to save time and effort when starting new projects.  See   .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-01\nValid as Of: 2024-03-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3356 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: In-app Help for the Action Editor is Available\nDescription: To make it easier to get help about specific UI elements, the action editor now features in-app help and can be accessed by clicking the question mark button .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-01\nValid as Of: 2024-03-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3357 ---\nComponent: Cloud Application Programming Model\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: February Release\nDescription: The February release of the SAP Cloud Application Programming Model is now available.   Highlights:    New common CDS definition for Timezones  Optimistic Locking API for Java  Convenience Options for cds bind  … and much more.  See February 2024 release for the CAP framework.   Action: We recommend to adapt the new versions as soon as possible, see Managing Dependencies.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-02-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3358 ---\nComponent: Availability Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Configuration of certificate chain validation\nDescription: Site24x7 Certificate monitors support now configuration of certificate chain validation option. Certificate chain validation is enabled by default but can now be switched off if necessary, e.g., in test scenarios with self-signed certificates or custom PKI setups.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-29\nValid as Of: 2024-02-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3359 ---\nComponent: Availability Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Introduction of quota on evaluations\nDescription: The creation of unlimited numbers of evaluations, independently of evaluation type has been restricted on group level. The following defaults apply:    AvS (cf-eu10-canary): 250 evaluations  AvS (cf-eu10): 500 evaluations    The existing setups get automatically 30% additional quota on top during the migration process to avoid disruption, if they already use more than 80% of the new default quota.  The onboarding processes to AvS have been adjusted to enable requests for additional quota on demand.   AvS (cf-eu10-canary): On", ". The following defaults apply:    AvS (cf-eu10-canary): 250 evaluations  AvS (cf-eu10): 500 evaluations    The existing setups get automatically 30% additional quota on top during the migration process to avoid disruption, if they already use more than 80% of the new default quota.  The onboarding processes to AvS have been adjusted to enable requests for additional quota on demand.   AvS (cf-eu10-canary): Onboarding of Monitors / Onboarding to AvS Canary  AvS (cf-eu10): Onboarding of Monitors / Onboarding to AvS eu10\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-29\nValid as Of: 2024-02-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3360 ---\nComponent: Availability Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Metric-based SLI monitors\nDescription: AvS introduces new evaluation types based on push testers that can be used to specify metric-based SLI monitors. Ypu're now able to push value, ratio, and good/total event occurrence metrics. You can map the metric measurements with a ruleset to states such as UP, DOWN, CRITICAL and TROUBLE. Additionally, you can configure ratio and event occurence metrics as the basis for availability calculations, such as success rate.   For more information, see the push metrics section in the REST API Reference.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-29\nValid as Of: 2024-02-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_ca2780e9383cc6273e2f529edc2f58762867d52fff03afd4f31ea8bd9856948b_v2"}